  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dxf_blocks_read",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "On the `new_object()` failure path, `dxf_blocks_read` frees the locally allocated `dxfname` even though `new_object` has already appended a `Dwg_Object` and stored that same pointer in `obj->dxfname`. It neither rolls back the object nor clears the field, leaving a dangling owned pointer. The subsequent critical-error cleanup calls `dwg_free`; for this pre-R13 drawing, `free_preR13_object` frees `obj->dxfname` again. The BLOCKS error cleanup should account for whether an object was appended, as the analogous ENTITIES/OBJECTS paths do.",
    "conditions": "A malformed input must be parsed as DXF and enter a BLOCKS section containing a recognized object/entity (the PoV creates a `BLOCK`). `dxf_blocks_read` duplicates the group-code-0 name, and `new_object` appends the object and assigns the duplicate to its `dxfname`, but malformed/truncated following pairs make `new_object` return NULL. `dxf_blocks_read` then frees the duplicate while the appended object remains in `dwg->object`; the critical parse error causes the harness to call `dwg_free`, which reaches the stale pointer and double-frees it. In the PoV, saved `idx` is 1 and `dwg->num_objects` becomes 2."
  },
